<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zollverein</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1834">1834</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as German Customs Union</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zollverein was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/customs-union">customs union</a> of German states led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a>, which came into force on 1 January 1834. It abolished tariffs between its members and set a common external tariff, eventually covering most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> but excluding <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>. By binding the smaller states economically to Prussia, it prepared the way for German unification in 1871.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zollverein.jpg" alt="Zollverein" width="320" height="271" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: User:52 Pickup · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map-GermanConfederation.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
